{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526489-v5-homebrew-baali-loresheet","id":1526489,"title":"(V5 Homebrew) Baali loresheet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-07T19:46:18-08:00","id":1526489,"title":"(V5 Homebrew) Baali loresheet","content":"Somewhat off the back of my attempt to make a Ventrue <i>antitribu</i> loresheet, I thought I'd poke around and see what I can figure out for everyone's favorite problematic lore blender bug-fuckers.<br /> <br /> <b>The Shaitan (Bloodline loresheet, any clan)</b><br /> <br /> Yeah we're all evil and shit! Not like all the other evil vampires, we're <i>double secret evil</i>! We got bugs, demons, bug-demons, demons but we try to keep them asleep, we're actually secret good guys all along, we're actually a bloodline of the Banu Haqim but only when we're not a bloodline of the Cappadocians or the Lasombra, but we don't count those, we have our hooks in every secret organization yet we're simultaneously nowhere, and we might have dubiously-canon accidentally either created or infiltrated the Banu Haqim anyways?<br /> <br /> ...I dunno, what fucking edition is this again? I don't know and neither do you, but we're not out to convert you like the Setites, we're out to convert you <i>and throw you into an organ pit!</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Devil in Disguise</b>: Millennia of being hunted by nearly every other clan and bloodline demands the ability to blend in, infiltrate, and move through the echelons of Kindred society unnoticed. Add two dice to any roll made to hide your true clan identity, or convince others you are of a clan not your own. If you possess any disciplines innate to the clan as which you are posing, your bonus is instead three dice.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Pleased to Meet You</b>: Sin knows sin, and no one knows sin like the Baali. If you do not already have access to the Auspex discipline, take Premonition at no cost -- you do not necessarily have the Auspex discipline, but rather a special power of your own. This power works like Premonition, except that it only works against mortals and gives insight into past sins mortals have committed, or plan to commit. If you do have (or later acquire) Auspex, you gain one to three bonus dice for uses of Auspex against mortals, depending upon how morally corrupt the target of your Auspex is (your Storyteller will decide).<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Psychomachia</b>: The Shaitan's growing connection to the powers below, and insight into sin and fear, empowers the use of their disciplines with hellish potency. When you use the Presence powers Awe, Daunt, Dread Gaze, Entrancement, or Majesty, or the Obfuscate powers Chimerstry or Fata Morgana, targets suffer a dice pool penalty to their resistance rolls equal to their current number of Stains, and their dice pool (after this reduction) cannot be higher than their Humanity.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Infernal Sorcery</b>: Whispers from below have instructed you in the use of powers beyond your own innate abilities. When you take this merit, choose either Blood Sorcery or Oblivion. If you start with this merit, you may start with dots in your chosen discipline as if it is innate to your clan. You count as attuned to that discipline, and no longer need to feed from the appropriate Resonance to raise its level with experience points (this has no impact on the experience cost to buy new levels if it is not innate to your clan).<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Hellborn Investiture</b>: Your connection to Hell and its ruling powers is such, you have gained a mote of their resistance and immortality. You only take Superficial damage from fire, halved as usual, instead of Aggravated. Moreover, you automatically succeed any roll to resist terror frenzy from fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T18:37:16-08:00","id":1528405,"title":"","content":"Ah, a man of culture!<br /> Never been into V5, but as one of the biggest fans on the bloodline ever, I thank you for your service!<br /> <img src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/FvxQ8L9WYAE5VbD.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T11:42:41-08:00","id":1528430,"title":"","content":"Not a big fan of the bloodline but I love the care you put into this lore sheet and how you made it for all clans to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T17:50:48-08:00","id":1528508,"title":"","content":"Thanks. One of my favorite PC's I've ever played was actually a Baali in a Dark Ages chronicle; I've had a fondness for them since, especially with the post-Revised edition lore involving the Molochim. But, I can definitely see why a lot of players don't like them for the &quot;turbo-edgelord&quot; factor, goofball lore, and inconsistency in representing them across editions and game lines. But still, unlike the 5th edition writers historically and currently, I do see value in adapting them to the new edition.<br /> <br /> I ran into two issues writing this one up: Daimonion, and how to represent them as a bloodline.<br /> <br /> Daimonion, unlike many proprietary disciplines, is (somehow) well-written. It's an eclectic and synergistic power set that fits with a holistic, relevant theme, while being powerful but not hopelessly overpowered. It's pretty much the model for how all proprietary disciplines should have been from the start. So, it was a little disheartening trying to figure out how to work Daimonion powers into the loresheet and v5's discipline framework -- not difficult by any means, but Daimonion was just such a fun discipline it hurt a little to break it up.<br /> <br /> If I had to compare it to anything in cWoD books, it's almost like a minor sphere where other disciplines' powers were cherry-picked and rebuilt to function inside a &quot;sin&quot; theme. Sense the Sin is a catch-all mini-Auspex that applies only to targets' sin and virtue. Fear of the Void is a sin-based Dread Gaze. Conflagration is a straight aggravated way to say &quot;go fuck yourself&quot; common to many disciplines. Psychomachia and Condemnation exist in this weird conjunction between Dementation, Dominate, and Chimerstry where they bear resemblance to each if you squint hard enough, but just barely.<br /> <br /> Looking at the library of v5 powers to date, almost every discipline with the right power and amalgam selection fits the bill seamlessly already. Just as one example, Unliving Hive (a level-3 power) would be the linchpin for the Avatars of the Swarm, forget the stomach-churning nastiness v5 tzimisce could do with it. It's just down to how one works with what's already there to bring the &quot;Baali&quot; flavor out.<br /> <br /> Considering what was done with the Hecata, it only makes sense to reimagine the Baali in the same vein, except as a mini-sect of nothing but apostates as opposed to disparate bloodlines. So that's what I did, and I think it's elegant enough faction flows from origin clan implicitly.<br /> <br /> I am considering alterations to the loresheet with what I've said about it in mind, though:<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Infernal Sorcery</b>: Whispers from below have instructed you in the use of powers beyond your own innate abilities. If you wish to learn the first dot of Blood Sorcery or Oblivion, you do not need to taste the blood of a vampire with either discipline. Additionally, you no longer need to feed from appropriate Resonances to raise Blood Sorcery or Oblivion with experience points (this has no impact on the experience cost to buy new levels if it is not innate to your clan). You may not start with dots in either, unless \u200bBlood Sorcery or Oblivion are innate to your clan or a dot would be granted by Predator Type.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Psychomachia</b>: The Shaitan's growing connection to the powers below, and insight into sin and fear, empowers the use of their disciplines against fellow Kindred with hellish potency. When you target another vampire with Animalism, Auspex, Dominate, Obfuscate, or Presence powers that are resisted by a contested roll, you may make an additional Rouse check when activating the power. If you do, your target may not roll more dice to resist that power than their Humanity rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T17:58:59-08:00","id":1528509,"title":"","content":"Also (to avoid spam shadowbanning, apologies for double-posting), this:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Devil in Disguise</b>: Millennia of being hunted by nearly every other clan and bloodline demands the ability to blend in, infiltrate, and move through the echelons of Kindred society unnoticed. Add two dice to any roll made to hide your true clan identity, or convince others you are of a clan not your own. Your Masks also apply towards other vampires, of effectiveness equivalent to their dot rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}